  <article class="prose-pillar" style="max-width: 760px;">
<h1>Child Safety Standards</h1>
<p>Last updated: October 8, 2026</p>
<p>These are the child safety standards for <strong>Pillar: Indian AI Girlfriend</strong>, the Android app published on Google Play by the developer <strong>Incline</strong> (package <code>com.incline.pillar</code>), and for this website, pillarapp.site. Together they are called "Pillar" below.</p>
<p>Pillar has <strong>zero tolerance for child sexual abuse and exploitation (CSAE)</strong> and child sexual abuse material (CSAM). This applies to every part of the service: chats, voice notes, voice calls, photos, characters and accounts.</p>

<h2>1. Pillar is for adults only</h2>
<ul>
<li>You must be 18 or older to use Pillar. This is a condition of our <a href="/terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.</li>
<li>Every Pillar AI girlfriend is an adult character. No character is, or may be presented as, under 18.</li>
<li>If we learn that an account belongs to someone under 18, we close it.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. What is prohibited</h2>
<p>On Pillar, no one may create, request, share, store or promote:</p>
<ul>
<li>Child sexual abuse material of any kind — real, drawn, edited or AI-generated images, video, audio or text.</li>
<li>Sexual or romantic content, roleplay or "age play" involving anyone under 18, or any character described as a minor or as childlike.</li>
<li>Requests asking an AI girlfriend to act, look or speak as a minor.</li>
<li>Grooming, sextortion, or any attempt to contact, meet or exploit a child.</li>
<li>Content that sexualises, normalises or encourages the abuse of children.</li>
<li>Trafficking of children or any links, contacts or instructions for finding CSAM.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. How we prevent it</h2>
<ul>
<li>Pillar's safety system watches for conversations involving minors. When it detects one, the AI girlfriend stops responding and the conversation is flagged to the Pillar team for review.</li>
<li>Photos sent by AI girlfriends depict adult characters only. Requests for images of minors are refused.</li>
<li>Attempts to get around these rules (for example, "jailbreaking" a character into childlike roleplay) are treated as violations.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. What happens when the rules are broken</h2>
<ul>
<li>We remove the content as soon as we know about it.</li>
<li>We permanently ban the account.</li>
<li>We keep the records the law requires us to keep, and share them only with the authorities.</li>
<li>We report it to the authorities, as described below.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Reporting to the authorities</h2>
<p>Pillar complies with the child safety laws that apply to it, including India's Protection of Children from Sexual Offences (POCSO) Act, 2012 and the Information Technology Act, 2000.</p>
<ul>
<li>In India, we report child sexual abuse material and child exploitation to the police and through the National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal (<a href="https://cybercrime.gov.in" rel="noopener" target="_blank">cybercrime.gov.in</a>).</li>
<li>Where a case involves another country, we report to the relevant authority there, including the National Center for Missing &amp; Exploited Children (NCMEC) CyberTipline in the United States.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. How to report a concern</h2>
<p>Anyone can report a child safety concern about Pillar — you do not need an account.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Inside the app:</strong> use the help and support option in the Pillar app to send us a report without leaving the app.</li>
<li><strong>By email:</strong> write to <a href="mailto:getinclined@gmail.com?subject=Child%20safety%20report">getinclined@gmail.com</a> with "Child safety" in the subject. Child safety reports are read first and acted on as a priority.</li>
</ul>
<p>Please do not attach or forward illegal images. Describe what you saw and where, and we will investigate.</p>
<p>If a child is in immediate danger, contact the police first: dial <strong>112</strong> in India, or call the Childline helpline on <strong>1098</strong>.</p>

<h2>7. Child safety contact</h2>
<p>Pillar has a designated child safety point of contact who handles reports and speaks with app stores and authorities about our child safety practices. Reach them at <a href="mailto:getinclined@gmail.com?subject=Child%20safety">getinclined@gmail.com</a>.</p>

<h2>8. Changes</h2>
<p>We review these standards as Pillar changes and update this page when they do.</p>

